ISO-10303-21;
/* Twi288: OPEN_SHELL with one ADVANCED_FACE on a PLANE (z=0, normal +Z); FACE_OUTER_BOUND references an EDGE_LOOP for a simple non-convex 5-vertex dart: four corners on a radius-5 circle, the fifth pulled in to the centre (0,0,0); FACE_BOUND references an EDGE_LOOP for a small inner triangle (hole) with one corner ALSO at (0,0,0); one VERTEX_POINT entity (#v_shared at (0,0,0)) IS referenced by both the outer dart wire (as an ordinary concave corner) and the inner triangle wire (as an ordinary corner); distinct geometry from Twi009 (unit square outer / offset square inner, pinch at (0.5,0.5)) — same mechanism, different shape and pinch location; STEP requires per-wire distinct VERTEX_POINTs — sharing IS the defect; kernel must split shared vertex into per-wire copies or reject as malformed */
HEADER;
FILE_DESCRIPTION(('Twi288'),'2;1');
